* AIP-20 vs ERC-20 vs ERC-7984
** Where the balance lives
*** ERC-20: public uint256 in contract storage
*** AIP-20: private notes (client side) + public u128
*** ERC-7984: FHE ciphertext handle (euint64)
** AIP-20 interface
*** Two balances per account
*** transfer_<from-domain>_to_<to-domain>
*** Commitments (partial notes)
*** mint_to_* / burn_* / total_supply
*** name / symbol / decimals
** Private transfer mechanics
*** Select notes, nullify, change note
*** 2 notes first, then 8 per recursion
*** "Balance too low" reverts
*** Recipient note delivered as encrypted log
** Authorization
*** ERC-20: approve / allowance / transferFrom
*** AIP-20: from + nonce, authwit, single use
*** ERC-7984: time-limited operator, any amount
** Failure and disclosure
*** ERC-20 and AIP-20 revert
*** ERC-7984 transfers zero silently
*** AIP-20 total supply is public
*** ERC-7984 disclose via decryption proof
** Compliance hooks
*** AIP-20: ARC-403 auth contract
*** ERC-7984: Restricted / Freezable extensions
*** ERC-20: _update override
